AB  - [SGMAY: cyber harm prominent in abstract] The digital context has become an integral part of society, transforming various aspects of human life. This research explores the Bangladesh perspective on rethinking human rights in the digital context. It also studies the challenges and opportunities arising from the rapid advancements in technology, internet access, and online activities in the country. The study investigates into the fundamental principles of human rights and their application in the digital realm, focusing on issues such as privacy, freedom of expression, access to information, and the right to be forgotten. It also highlights the risks associated with the misuse of digital technologies, including surveillance, online harassment, cyberbullying, and censorship. The study emphasizes the importance of multi-stakeholder collaboration to develop comprehensive policies and frameworks that protect human rights while fostering digital innovation. The research concludes by advocating for a rights-based approach to tackle the evolving challenges in the digital era and enable individuals to fully exercise their rights in the digital society.
