AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] Bangladesh is one of the fastest-growing internet consumer bases in the world. Within a very short period, the country reached millions of internet and cell phone subscribers. The growth comes with economic prosperity as well. Bangladesh ranked 41st among the economies in the world. However, with the economic growth, the country is also being transformed into a hybrid regime from a democratic country under the present Awami League government. The ruling party has adopted many laws and used the state apparatus to oppress dissent and opposition. The government adopted the Digital Security Act (DSA) 2018 to suppress and censor the information flow in the cyber world. This chapter focuses on how the government and government supporters in the country are using the Act in the name of fighting cybercrime. And the chapter also aims at connecting the traits of the hybrid regime with the present state of freedom of speech in Bangladesh.
