AB  - [SGINC: on-topic (law, speech or online harm)] Significance For financially motivated groups, banks have become a particularly popular target for cyber intrusions and scams. Although the financial sector has made significant improvements to its cybersecurity since the 2016 theft of hundreds of millions of dollars from Bangladesh Bank via the SWIFT system, banks continue to face a diverse and evolving array of threats online. Impacts Cybercriminals will rely more on QR-code based scams to evade email spam detectors. Generative AI tools will be actively used to steal cryptocurrencies. Banks will implement stronger security controls for individual users and flag more online transactions for review.
