AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] The rapid expansion of digital technologies, online financial systems, and internet-basedcommunication has significantly increased the incidence of cybercrime in India. UttarPradesh, being one of the most populous states, faces substantial challenges related tocyber fraud, identity theft, ransomware attacks, financial scams, cyberstalking, and digitalmisinformation. Traditional policing methods are increasingly inadequate for addressing thecomplexity and speed of cybercriminal activities. In this context, Artificial Intelligence (AI) hasemerged as a transformative tool in cybercrime management and modern policing. This research paper examines the role of Artificial Intelligence in cybercrime management withspecial reference to the emerging strategies adopted by Uttar Pradesh Police. The studyexplores AI-based surveillance systems, predictive policing, machine learning algorithms, digital forensics, facial recognition systems, and automated cyber threat detection Mechanisms. The paper also analyzes institutional challenges such as lack of technical Infrastructure, ethical concerns, privacy issues, shortage of trained personnel, and legal constraints in implementing AI-based policing systems. Using a qualitative and analytical research methodology, the study evaluates the effectiveness of AI technologies in strengthening cybercrime prevention, investigation, and response mechanisms. The findings suggest that AI-based policing can significantly enhance operational efficiency, crime prediction accuracy, and public safety if supported by appropriate policy frameworks, technological investments, and ethical regulations. The paper concludes that Uttar Pradesh Police can become a model for smart policing in India by integrating Artificial Intelligence with community participation, cyber awareness programs, and modern governance principles.
