AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] The increasing prevalence of cybercrimes has become a significant concern for both governmental authorities and citizens. This research investigates the trends in various types of cybercrimes, including Credit/Debit Card frauds, ATM frauds, Online Banking frauds, OTP frauds, and other types of frauds, across different states and Union Territories (UTs) of India from 2018 to 2022. By applying One-Way Analysis of Variance (ANOVA), we compare the distributions of cyber crimes across regions to assess whether mean crime rates differ significantly across states and UTs. The results aim to inform policymakers about regional variations and potential areas for targeted interventions in cybersecurity.
