AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] The fast-growing use of deepfake in India has become a pressing issue of concern to the digital governance, privacy rights, and democratic integrity. This paper explores the changing legal environment surrounding the issue of deepfake media covered in the proposed Digital India Act and Information Technology laws. Based on the recent legal rulings, legislative developments, and international precedent, this in-depth discussion of the multi-layered liability regime involving creators, distributors, and digital intermediaries explores various facets of digital travel liability. The paper assesses the overlap of constitutional rights, the provisions of criminal law, the principles of data protection, and the accountability mechanisms of platforms and considers the technological and jurisdictional issues in the regulation of AI-produced synthetic media.
