JO  - International Conference on Intelligent and Innovative Technologies in Computing, Electrical and Electronics (IITCEE)
DO  - https://doi.org/10.1109/iitcee67948.2026.11394673
AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] With the rapid increase in cybercrime cases such as UPI frauds, sextortion, OTP scams, and fake social media accounts, many victims remain hesitant to report incidents due to privacy concerns, low digital literacy, language barriers, and fear of retaliation. Traditional cybercrime reporting portals are often form-heavy, text-based, and available in limited languages, which further discourages reporting. CrimeScanAI is a user-centric, AI-powered cybercrime reporting assistant designed to simplify this process. The system accepts complaints via text, voice, or image input, supports multiple Indian languages, and uses Optical Character Recognition (OCR) and Natural Language Processing (NLP) to extract key details like scam type, date, amount, and contact information. CrimeScanAI automatically generates a structured FIR draft and provides a dashboard for law enforcement to review, categorize, and respond to complaints efficiently. By combining accessibility, multilingual support, and AI-driven automation, CrimeScanAI aims to empower citizens, improve reporting rates, and assist authorities in faster and more accurate cybercrime investigations.
