AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] Over the past few years, India's payment industry has witnessed a remarkable evolution in the digital payment landscape, and these developments are poised to continue in the years ahead.Solutions in this regard are mostly the Unified payment interface (UPI) and others.The ultimate user experience for swift, convenient and cashless payments.But, the technology has also increased the number of online financial frauds and cybercrimes.Fraudsters take advantage of the loopholes in digital platforms by using phishing, fake payment requests, QR code scams, identity theft, OTP frauds, and social engineering techniques.Mobile banking and digital wallets have become a leading cause of financial risks with the advent of UPI scams.With the rise of mobile banking and digital wallets, UPI scams have become one of the biggest threats to financial security.The present study critically explores the legal framework pertaining to online financial frauds in India focusing on the UPI scams.It examines the impact of legislations like the Information Technology Act, 2000, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, Reserve Bank of India guidelines and banking regulations on combating digital crimes.The Study also examines issues in investigation, enforcement, consumer awareness and cyber security measures, and recommends changes to enhance the overall legal framework and cyber payment security in India.
