AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] This chapter contains a comparative analysis of how four jurisdictions (the European Union, the United States, China, and India) deal with the regulation of deepfakes. It will compare their definitions of synthetically generated content, the assignment of liability for platforms, and how each jurisdiction pursues innovation and harm prevention. This chapter will also look at industry-led initiatives to combat deepfakes like the Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity (C2PA), and platform-level labeling. Ultimately, this analysis shows that while regulatory activity is continuing to grow across borders, enforcement gaps, definition inconsistencies, and the rapid rate of technological change continue to exceed the capacity of the legal system to keep pace with these changes.
