AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] The rapid development of deepfake technology synthetic media created by artificial intelligence to convincingly imitate human appearance and behaviour poses a structural problem to the global legal order. Beyond being a mere advancement in disinformation, deepfakes represent a fundamental challenge to the epistemic trust upon which democratic, legal, and diplomatic processes rely. By enabling low-cost, high-impact deception, they exploit the grey zones of digital governance, complicating principles of cyber sovereignty and making it difficult to attribute wrongful acts in the digital sphere.
