AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] In our fast-moving digital world, smart devices have become a part of everyday life—from the gadgets in our homes to the machines in our hospitals. But as these devices become smarter, so do the threats they face. With the rise of artificial intelligence, cybercriminals are now using powerful tools to launch highly sophisticated attacks, especially targeting devices connected to the Internet of Things (IoT). This study looks closely at how AI is changing the cybercrime landscape in India. By analyzing real-world cases and patterns, we explore which devices are most at risk, the types of AI-driven attacks being used, and how long it takes to detect them. We also examine how effective India’s current cyber laws are in dealing with these modern threats. What we find is clear: not all devices are equally vulnerable, and our defense strategies need to evolve just as fast as the technology itself.
