AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] With the rise in globalization, the socioeconomic and cultural facets of life have been tremendously affected. The chapter shall deal with the analysis of cybercrime under the Information and Technology Act of India. As much as the Internet has brought glorious changes in our lives, it has led to several crimes leading to huge losses. Anything and everything associated with the web world is governed under “cyberlaw.” The word “cyber” means “relating to or characteristic of the culture of computers, information technology, and virtual reality.” The origin of the word “cyber” is from “cybernetics.” Cyberlaw, under the IT Act 2000, rose as it intended to control the violations happening in the cyber world. The author shall also focus on the scenario of intermediaries around the world and India. It covers the international treaties, conventions, statutes, etc. formulated for the protection of the rights of the creator. The researcher through this thesis will also throw light on various other loopholes of the IT Act and cyberlaw and recommendations to combat the same and highlight the concept of intermediary in its various aspects discussed in the different literature by various authors and judicial officers.
