AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] This paper explores a connection between low computer literacy and cybercrime victimization in Jharkhand, which is one of the socio-economically deprived states in India. We estimated the probability of susceptibility to cybercrime as a binary outcome of logistic regression analysis based on the data that was collected by performing structured surveys conducted in 24 districts. Findings indicated that 46.2% of participants were victims, and the low level of digital skills is closely associated with a low awareness of online dangers. The predictive model achieved an accuracy of 55.5%, highlighting the need for more advanced modelling approaches. The generated results also make a great case as to why swift policy intervention is necessary in the digital area of marginalized groups resided in Jharkhand, to limit the danger of cybercrimes.
