AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] Through this chapter, the authors seek to critically analyse the legal framework dealing with issues pertaining to money laundering in the online gambling landscape. The chapter in the context of the book will deal with aspects of money laundering in online gambling since it has a significant impact on the financial services and the economy of India. In the Introduction section of the chapter, the authors will provide an elaboration of the growth and development of online gambling in India in the context of the pandemic and rapid investments in the space. The Non-Uniformity of Gambling Legislations Across the Nation section of the chapter will focus on the legislative framework in detail in India while dealing with online gambling (both central and state) and the legal apparatus existing in India. The authors will flag how the Indian regulatory apparatus is ill-equipped to handle money laundering through online gambling intermediaries due to innovative techniques adopted by offenders such as chip dumping, etc. In The Legal Landscape in India section of the chapter, the authors will decipher the legislative framework existing in other jurisdictions viz. the United Kingdom, the United States of America, and the European Union. The part is an attempt at drawing a comparison of the practices in these jurisdictions (i.e., regulatory practices such as Risk-Based Approach, Application of Internal Controls, Customer Verification, Due Diligence, and Employee Training, etc.) with the Indian framework. The part will serve as a roadmap for the legislature to evolve a framework in India for combatting money laundering in the sector.
