AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] “Technology and crime make deadly combination. We are drenched in silicon and living on borrowed time where technology is the master and humanity its servant. It is said,”….The modern thief can steal more with a computer than with a gun. Tomorrow's terrorist may be able to do more damage with a keyboard than with a bomb". Computers at risks’,(National Research Council, National Academy Press.1991) 1. INTRODUCTION: Cyber crimes have again taken a boon and set in a discourse as to whether a new legislation is needed to deal with them or existing legal regime like Indian Penal Code and Information Technology Act is flexible enough to effectively deal with this new type of hybrid crimes done by techno savvy people of high intellect. One school of thought thinks that cyber crime are not in any way dissimilar to the ordinary crimes like trespass, larceny or conspiracy with a difference that a computer has been used as a medium or instrument for commission of crime as the Fundamentals of crime are : Watkins is of the opinion that the hard evidence of the extent of such crimes and the need for specific legislation directed at computer crime is still lacking. See Watkins, Computer crime: Seperating the Myth from reality , C.A. Magazine, January1981.
