AB  - [SGINC: on-topic] Life for an Indian girl in the public domain is a challenge. She is haunted and -traumatised through a form of school-based bullying, and more cyberbullying, which masks the deep-rooted issue of 'eve-teasing'. Bullying is an aggressive, intentional act or behaviour which is usually carried out by an individual or a group of individuals repeatedly over time against a victim who is not able to easily defend him or her. At the beginning of the study, participants were provided with detailed information about bullying and the various acts which constitute bullying. Four co-educational schools in Punjab, one each from the categories of rural school, urban lower SES school, urban middle SES school, and urban high SES school, were approached for the purpose of data collection. Teachers and school counsellors were requested to nominate female students who, according to the available evidence or school records, or from their own observation, had been known to experience bullying.
